{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 66, :comments ["<b>My name is YHWH</b> — It is like \"your name,\" as in <i>and to Moses He said, go up to YHWH</i> (Exodus 24:1)."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The verse phrase 'my name is YHWH' (שמי ה') is read as equivalent to a construct form meaning 'your name'; the Exodus parallel is cited as an analogy of a name attached to a divine referent."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:01.060778Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}